# No export-only barrels

Do **not** add `index.ts` (or any file) whose only job is re-exporting from sibling modules.

## Forbidden

```ts
// features/auth/login/index.ts — ❌ delete; import login-page directly
export { LoginPage } from './login-page';

// services/auth/index.ts — ❌
export * as authQuery from './auth.query';

// components/form/index.ts — ❌
export { TextField } from './text-field';
```

## Do instead

```ts
// app/(auth)/sign-in/page.tsx
import { LoginPage } from '@/features/auth/login/login-page';

// feature code
import * as authQuery from '@/services/auth/auth.query';
import { TextField } from '@/components/form/text-field';
```

## Workspace packages (`@wichat/*`)

- Point `package.json` `"exports"` at the **implementation file** (`provider.tsx`, `create-api-client.ts`, …), not a re-export shim.
- Use subpath exports when consumers need another module (`@wichat/i18n/locale`, `@wichat/api-client/api-error`).
- **`@wichat/contracts`:** `src/index.ts` is allowed only because it **defines** schemas/types in place (not a passthrough barrel).

## App integrations

- Prefer a named file (e.g. `integrations/api-client.ts`) over `integrations/api-client/index.ts` when the module is a single singleton.
